---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { repoUrl } from "../site";
---

<Base
  title="License"
  description="LibreDental is released under the Apache License, Version 2.0."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>License</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      LibreDental is free software, released under the
      <a href="https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0">Apache License, Version 2.0</a>.
    </p>

    <div class="card license-notice">
      <p>Copyright 2026 The LibreDental contributors</p>
      <p>
        Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the "License"); you may
        not use this software except in compliance with the License. You may
        obtain a copy of the License at
        <a href="https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0">https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, software
        distributed under the License is distributed on an "AS IS" BASIS,
        WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied.
        See the License for the specific language governing permissions and
        limitations under the License.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p>
      The full license text is also in the
      <a href={`${repoUrl}/blob/main/LICENSE`}><code>LICENSE</code> file</a>
      in the source repository.
    </p>

    <h2>In short</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>You may use LibreDental for any purpose, including commercially.</li>
      <li>You may study, modify, and redistribute the source.</li>
      <li>
        Redistributions must keep the copyright notice and license text, and
        say which files were changed.
      </li>
      <li>The license includes a patent grant from contributors.</li>
      <li>It does not grant rights to the LibreDental name or logo.</li>
      <li>Provided as-is, without warranty.</li>
    </ul>

    <p class="muted">
      This summary is a plain-language overview, not legal advice. If it ever
      differs from the license itself, the license is what counts.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party components</h2>
    <p>
      LibreDental is built on open-source libraries that keep their own
      licenses. They are listed in the repository's <code>go.mod</code> and
      <code>frontend/package.json</code>.
    </p>

    <h2>Trademarks</h2>
    <p>
      LibreDental™ is a trademark claiming common law rights. The LibreDental
      name and logo are trademarks of the LibreDental project.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
